":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.05401242015775387,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.0,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"argenx SE, a commercial-stage biopharma company, develops various therapies for the treatment of autoimmune diseases in the United States, Japan, China, the Netherlands, and internationally. The company offers VYVGART for the treatment of gMG and immune thrombocytopenia (ITP), and VYVGART HYTRULO for the treatment of gMG and chronic inflammatory demyelinating polyneuropathy (CIDP). It also develops efgartigimod for the treatment of seronegative gMG, ocular myasthenia gravis (MG), primary ITP, grave's disease, myositis, Sj\u00f6gren's disease, systemic sclerosis, and AMR; empasiprubart for MMN, delayed graft function, and CIDP; and adimanebart for congenital myasthenic syndrome and spinal muscular atrophy. In addition, the company is developing ARGX-213, a neonatal Fc receptor (FcRn)-targeted antibody engineered for half-life extension and sustained IgG reduction; ARGX-124, a FcRn pipeline candidate; ARGX-109, which targets IL-6 to treat inflammation; ARGX-121, which targets immunoglobulin A; and ARGX-118, which develops antibodies against Galectin-10, as well as cusatuzumab, ARGX-112, ARGX-114, and ARGX-115. It has strategic partnerships and license agreements with Zai Lab to develop and commercialize efgartigimod; Halozyme Therapeutics to its ENHANZE for the prevention and treatment of human diseases; OncoVerity, Inc for cusatuzumab; and AbbVie, Inc. for ARGX-115. argenx SE was incorporated in 2008 and is based in Amsterdam, the Netherlands.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Karen  Massey | CEO & Executive Director | Age 46 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Each employee generates $364K of free cash flow annually.","financial_summary":["argenx SE is a large-cap healthcare business with a $58.3B market cap.","The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are contracting by -271.7pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at -20% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $679M in free cash flow, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.53\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -271.7pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Price sits 588% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":5.882247737959718},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +7.0% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"INVESTOR ALERT: Pomerantz Law Firm Investigates Claims On Behalf of Investors of argenx SE - ARGX","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/investor-alert-pomerantz-law-firm-investigates-claims-on-behalf-of-investors-of-argenx-se---argx-302931433.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793925720.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.447,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"Best Biotech Stocks to Buy Now as AI Stocks Tank: ARGX","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/commentary/3023442/best-biotech-stocks-to-buy-now-as-ai-stocks-tank-argx?cid=CS-ZC-FT-investment_ideas-3023442","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793828520.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.637,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"argenex SE (NASDAQ:ARGX) Stock Rated \u201cModerate Buy\u201d by Sell-Side Brokerages","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/argenex-se-nasdaqargx-stock-rated-moderate-buy-by-sell-side-brokerages.